## 4. Search Tree (rooted at Nairobi)

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Nairobi (0)"] --> B["Thika (45)"]
    A --> C["Naivasha (90)"]
    B --> D["Nyeri (158)"]
    C --> E["Nakuru (160)"]
    E --> F["Kericho (266)"]
    E --> G["Eldoret (316)"]
    F --> H["Kisumu (351) — GOAL"]
    G --> I["Kisumu (433) — GOAL"]

    style H fill:#1D9E75,color:#fff
    style I fill:#F0997B,color:#000
```

Numbers in parentheses are cumulative path cost (distance so far) from Nairobi. Paths that return to an already-visited town are pruned. The Thika → Nyeri branch (Central Highlands) does not lead to Kisumu in this graph, so it is a dead end relative to the goal.

## 5. Optimal Path: Nairobi → Kisumu (Uniform-Cost Search)

Since distance is the path cost function, this is solved with Uniform-Cost Search (equivalent to Dijkstra's algorithm): the node with the lowest cumulative cost is always expanded next, and the search stops only when the goal is **expanded**, not when it is first added to the frontier.

### Step-by-step expansion

| Step | Node expanded | Cumulative cost (km) | Frontier after expansion |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Nairobi | 0 | Thika: 45, Naivasha: 90 |
| 2 | Thika | 45 | Naivasha: 90, Nyeri: 158 |
| 3 | Naivasha | 90 | Nyeri: 158, Nakuru: 160 |
| 4 | Nyeri | 158 | Nakuru: 160 (Nyeri has no new successors — dead end) |
| 5 | Nakuru | 160 | Kericho: 266, Eldoret: 316 |
| 6 | Kericho | 266 | Eldoret: 316, Kisumu: 351 |
| 7 | Eldoret | 316 | Kisumu: 351 (the path via Eldoret reaches Kisumu at 433, which is worse, so it is discarded) |
| 8 | **Kisumu** | **351** | Goal expanded — stop |

### Candidate paths compared

| Route | Calculation | Total distance |
|---|---|---|
| Nairobi → Naivasha → Nakuru → **Kericho** → Kisumu | 90 + 70 + 106 + 85 | **351 km** ✅ |
| Nairobi → Naivasha → Nakuru → Eldoret → Kisumu | 90 + 70 + 156 + 117 | 433 km |

### Conclusion

The optimal path from Nairobi to Kisumu is:

**Nairobi → Naivasha → Nakuru → Kericho → Kisumu — Total distance: 351 km**

Uniform-Cost Search expands Eldoret (316 km) before Kisumu because it is cheaper at that point, but the route through Eldoret only reaches Kisumu at 433 km. The 351 km route via Kericho therefore stays the cheapest on the frontier and is returned as the optimal path, 82 km shorter than the alternative.

